Concrete execution now returns the expected Boolean for every prompt example and several boundary cases. For the symbolic proof, I’m using a ghost function that denotes the first term in `P, P*n, P*n², …` reaching or passing `x`; the loop invariant proves the program returns true exactly when that term equals `x`.
apply patch
